1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,570
The trial run began at the clinic with a physical test and a commitment: one month, three sessions a week, and a written log.

2
00:00:08,570 --> 00:00:12,864
“Your body is not a bank,” the doctor said.

3
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:28,560
“You cannot borrow sleep at a deficit and pay it back with an egg.” The attitude of the whole team was measured at the door: who was able to come, who came at the hour available, and who came only to be seen.

4
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:34,494
At the counter you could buy a dish of food, but not a rest.

5
00:00:34,494 --> 00:00:38,048
The movement of the class was slow and open.

6
00:00:38,048 --> 00:00:46,936
A national coach, a physiotherapist, and a student with a disability designed a session for a comfortable range of motion.

7
00:00:46,936 --> 00:00:50,625
“Pain is information,” she said.

8
00:00:50,625 --> 00:01:05,107
“Fatigue is a bill.” The strain on the knee, the tension in the belt, and the weakness in the posture were all written down, and the pressure to return too early was noted beside them.

9
00:01:05,107 --> 00:01:07,751
The mental part was harder.

10
00:01:07,751 --> 00:01:19,733
The absence of sleep had produced a reaction that no one had predicted: a short temper, a fixation on weight, and a hunting instinct for someone to blame.

11
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:24,167
“You are ill if you cannot rest,” the doctor said.

12
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:34,655
“That is not a weakness of character.” A butterfly on the window and a frog in the yard were the only patients who did not argue.

13
00:01:34,655 --> 00:01:43,677
The accommodation was a room in the attic of the sports center, with a vessel of water and a colony of pigeons above the stadium.

14
00:01:43,677 --> 00:01:53,830
“You may stay here,” the manager said, “but maybe you should go home.” Perhaps the strain was ours, not his.

15
00:01:53,830 --> 00:02:02,778
Our task was to make the training tiring in a good way, and to keep the exertion inside a tolerable range.

16
00:02:02,778 --> 00:02:11,341
The connexion between the mouth and the mind was the lesson of the month: what he said about his own pain was not what he felt.

17
00:02:11,341 --> 00:02:22,843
Across the four weeks, the numbers told a story of improvised rest, a colon of small statistics, and one injury that could have been prevented.

18
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:31,261
Together they wrote the second protocol, and the first line was: follow the foot, not the clock.

19
00:02:31,261 --> 00:02:43,368
The stress of the schedule and the worried faces at the door told the same story; the mentality of “more is better” was the hardest habit to face, in a group or alone.

20
00:02:43,368 --> 00:02:50,585
They had to be tolerant with the people who came late, and firm with the plan.
